      "published_at": "2026-11-23T22:50:49+00:00",
      "text": "🇦🇱 🇱🇾 🇺🇦 The Albanian Foreign Ministry denied claims that drones were launched from its territory for a terrorist attack in Libya. The Albania claim was first spread by Clash Report, an Istanbul-based news account reportedly run by a media company tied to Turkish government-aligned outlets. Turkey backs the Tripoli-based government, a rival of the authorities in Benghazi. Earlier, Ukraine claimed responsibility for the terrorist attack at the port of Benghazi. Deputy Chairman of the Presidential Council of Libya al-Kuni called these actions equivalent to a declaration of war on the Libyan state. 🔴 @DDGeopolitics",
